+### D-141 · 2026-08-30 · Provenance and immutable evidence now fail closed at every reconstructed identity
+
+**Decision:** the post-audit implementation hardens four evidence boundaries without changing a scientific statistic or frozen constant. `git_state()` now treats any failed Git subprocess as unknown/dirty, ignores stdout from failed commands, and defaults provenance to the repository containing the installed source rather than the caller's current directory; explicit repository arguments remain explicit. New run records duplicate `fit_id`, while historical schema-v2 records that omitted only that duplicate remain readable by reconstructing it from their exact `Config`. `load_runs()` reconstructs every config type-sensitively, cross-checks all unit/config/run/fit/stage/seed copies, refuses truthy policy substitutes, requires an exact requested run inventory including metric rows, and checks exact clean/trustworthy Git booleans when requested. `ConfirmatoryRuns` binds and revalidates its run/config/unit/fit identity snapshot so a mutable DataFrame cannot change identities after crossing the critic-loading boundary.
+
+**Serialized and frozen evidence:** gate verdict records now carry the complete source row behind every disagreement, recompute its digest/value/normalisation, and bind every run record to the manifest's exact clean commit. Older detached serialized verdicts that lack source rows are refused; the immutable certified filesystem attempt still verifies and recomputes unchanged. Threshold recomputation now binds every cell to the registered baseline unit, exact `Config`/`fit_id`, member roster, clean Git state, and one common commit before reproducing the permanently frozen scalar. C-005 public type/seed guards were also closed before hashing or sorting malformed input.
+
+**Verification:** focused gate/threshold suite **190 passed**; combined changed-subsystem suite **465 passed, 1 skipped**; full clean suite **1,205 passed, 4 skipped in 412.07 s**. No calibration, label, real data, reserve unit, registered constant, or experimental fit was created.
+
+**Plan ref:** P§10.1, P§13.5.1; D-033, D-034, D-054, D-059, D-072, D-103, D-109, D-139, D-140. **Reviewed by Sol:** **not yet — delta 67.**
+
+### D-142 · 2026-08-30 · Owner-authorised Sol2 Week 6 readiness build, without scientific execution
+
+**Decision:** the student explicitly designated the active Codex implementation agent **"Sol2"**, asked it to work with external Sol instead of the historical local labels Fable/Oups, and authorised pulling Week 6 readiness forward (DEV-015). The label changes no governance authority: **external Sol remains the adversarial reviewer/certifier**, and this work is presented for review rather than described as Sol-certified.
+
+**Built against S§W6, using synthetic/stubbed execution only:** (1) `run_repair_condition()` executes one unit/seed as baseline + data repair + exactly one registered model repair, sharing one evaluation scale and refusing zero or multiple model-repair arms before fitting; it is a one-condition harness, not the twenty-seed acceptance verdict. (2) `labels.py` implements Plan Table 2's exact pure mapping and four-way counts, while stating structurally that booleans are not evidence and the real run-to-label adapter remains absent. (3) `CriticDataset` physically separates allowlisted `X`, labels `y`, and grouping metadata, recursively copies nested values, and exposes only `X` to the model. (4) `batch.py` gives the 150 unique Experiment-1 computations an immutable fit-identity manifest, per-fit directories, append-only fsynced transitions, crash-window recovery, failure isolation, result digests, and prefix-only durable sync. It refuses partial immutable fits, divergent remote history, malformed identities, and the entire default Experiment-1 launch before compute because 30 fits carry two scientific roles that the current runner cannot yet record from one fit.
+
+**Not done or claimed:** no Kaggle API/session, no real Experiment-1 launch, no repair acceptance verdict, no repair-derived label, no exclusion-rate observation, no registered split seed/targets/floors, and no change to `constants.py`. The methodology chapter's explicit fixed-10× same-process wording remains a student prose obligation. **Reviewed by Sol:** **not yet — delta 67.**
+
+### D-143 · 2026-08-30 · Week 6 launch inventory exposes two scientific blockers; the runner refuses to guess
+
+**Finding:** the registered 300-unit design cannot yet supply the schedule's two-repair label protocol uniformly. **173/300 units have no model-repair arm and 127/300 have exactly one**; among the fifteen canonical repair-validation units, **7 lack** a model repair and **8 have exactly one**. Separately, **30/150 Experiment-1 baseline fits also discharge `repair_validation`** under D-033. A stage-only batch would train those computations twice; one-role records would fail to show that one fit discharged both obligations. The new plan deduplicates on `fit_id` and refuses the default launch until a multi-role recorder is ruled and implemented. For ordinary units, 285 have `exp3_repairs` repair obligations but no matching baseline obligation under that role, so the future evidence adapter cannot honestly infer labels from the existing role inventory.
+
+**Decision:** do not choose a model-repair intervention, fabricate a missing baseline role, duplicate a shared fit, or launch confirmatory compute from these gaps. Sol is asked to rule: (a) which registered model repair applies to the 173 units, including the seven canonical units; (b) the record contract by which one fit may emit multiple obligation records without pretending to be multiple executions; (c) whether interrupted within-fit state is quarantined/restarted or requires resumable model checkpoints; and (d) when real Week 6 execution is authorised. Until then, Week 6 is **infrastructure-ready in part, scientifically launch-blocked, and not complete**.
+
+**Data/compute:** registry introspection and tests only; no scientific value inspected or produced. **Plan ref:** P§7.2–7.5, P Table 2, S§W6, D-033, D-087, D-096, D-139. **Reviewed by Sol:** **not yet — delta 67.**
